## What Problem This Solves

Preserves regression coverage for required commands that remain pending when execution times out or the caller aborts. Main already owns the startup-clock fix; this PR keeps the shared fixture and its Gateway policy, recovered-dashboard, and hidden-tool cases.

## User Impact

Developers retain coverage of normal completion, execution-budget expiry, caller cancellation, and cleanup when a tool response rejects. Production behavior is unchanged.

## Why This Change Was Made

Rebased onto main `164c0dba58183af1be4b4af3b431b1a4fed6b021`, preserving the effective fixes from the previous merge commits. The required-command cases join both the response and attempt before closing the controlled process fixture. In the fixture, everything outside that case block is identical to this main.

The change adds exactly 58 net test lines plus a separate `config/test-lines-allocations/pr-167409-required-command.txt` allocation of 58 for the distinct cancellation regressions and reliable cleanup. The shared baseline scalar is unchanged.

## Evidence

- Head: `7dba4354949cb0fda19baf09ee0c0a482ee82650`; tested tree: `fc715df8fa5293b436bd8c2d3fd301e5a3f04ef0`.
- Fresh frozen-lockfile installation and all checks ran serially in an isolated Linux environment with Node 26.12.1 and pinned pnpm 12.15.0.
- Focused canonical test: **18/18 PASS**, command wall **402.61s**, Vitest **385.12s**, including rebuilt compiled workers and production-path module loading. This retains main's existing startup/recovery coverage and uses virtual waiting for the pending-command boundary.
- Extension-test typecheck: **PASS** (**148.89s**).
- Targeted typed lint including pinned Bun parity: **PASS**, **0 warnings / 0 errors** (**344.76s**).
- Targeted oxfmt, whitespace checks and timeout-race ratchet: **PASS**.
- Canonical test-line checker: **PASS** (**33.68s**): 6,564,230 lines / ceiling 6,564,387 / slack 157. Upstream repaired the renewed budget debt before this refresh. The earlier exact-Git-LF preflight was followed by this actual checker run. This PR's allocation remains exactly its own +58 LF growth; no shared scalar or ignore was raised.
- Fresh independent static P0–P2 review covered this immutable candidate and the current production cancellation contract: **no actionable findings**. No formal AutoReview clean report or new live-model lifecycle execution is claimed.
- This exact head's [CI run 42394706803](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/42394706803) and [openclaw/ci-gate](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/42394706803/job/128471257510) completed **SUCCESS**: 53 jobs, 20 successful and 33 conditionally skipped, zero failures or cancellations. The published ci-gate commit status is also successful. No earlier-head CI is counted as proof for this refresh.
- The [hosted fixture job](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/42394706803/job/128469822015) ran the same file using pinned Bun: **1 file / 18 tests PASS**, Vitest **71.05s**, test step wall **76s**, job wall **136s**. These are elapsed times, not a billing estimate.

Related: #148397. The descriptions and native lifecycle traces below are historical, belong to their named older heads, and do not certify this rebased candidate.

<details><summary>Previous description and historical evidence</summary>

## Current conflict repair (2026-10-18)

Updated candidate: `5d318f3c10651211418c855f6dfa62d67b887a7b`.

Resolves the conflict with main `ca5ac6f5b69aa8704b653fade36e2fa59937c7fb` in `extensions/codex/src/app-server/run-attempt.dynamic-tools.test.ts` through a normal merge. Production code is unchanged.

The resolution uses main's shared `startTool` fixture and fake clock, retains its AutoReview lifetime/replay cases, and preserves this PR's required-command completion, execution-timeout, caller-abort, and cleanup coverage. Main already owns the startup clock fix; the resolution does not add a second clock owner.

Relative to that main, exactly one test file changes: 64 additions and 6 deletions.

Validation of the resolved tree:
- Focused test file: **12/12 passed**. Command wall time **128.83s**, Vitest **119.32s**, including cold worker compilation. Node **26.3.0**, pinned pnpm **12.11.1**, frozen lockfile. Node ran after the optional pinned Bun staging hit a local cache permission error.
- Formatting, `git diff --check`, and the test timeout-race ratchet passed.
- Independent read-only review found no blocking defects; the cancellation mapping was checked against the production owner. The canonical AutoReview helper completed preparation only; no validated AutoReview report is claimed.
- Full extension-test typecheck passed (423.14s). Targeted typed lint passed. The earlier typecheck attempt stopped on an active task-owned artifact lock and was rerun after its owner finished. Updated-head hosted CI is pending; no earlier-head CI is counted as proof for this commit.

The evidence below is historical and belongs to its named older heads. It does not certify this resolved tree. No merge, force push, deployment, or GitHub comment is part of this repair.

<details>
<summary>Prior PR description and historical evidence</summary>

## What Problem This Solves

Fixes required-command Codex tests expiring during startup before native execution begins on slower Linux CI.

## User Impact

Developers retain deterministic coverage of pending required commands, deadline cancellation and caller cancellation. This is a test-only change; production behavior is unchanged.

## Why This Change Was Made

Own Date and timers before creating the attempt, retain main's 10ms yield and 20ms virtual pending wait with the default 5-second attempt budget, and preserve all three completion/cancellation cases. Cleanup aborts outstanding work and waits for both the response and attempt before closing the host and command, including when the response rejects.

The branch incorporates frozen main `24ca81d55bce94b26cb5c494e6987c39f2276081` through a normal two-parent merge commit, preserving its history. Relative to that main, only `extensions/codex/src/app-server/run-attempt.dynamic-tools.test.ts` changes (64 additions, 6 deletions).

## Evidence

- Updated candidate: `e2d5fa603e2f8ba3e353f9e6d8d98e218ac69d3f`; fixture SHA256 `dbac3f89cb0dcab83a11c458956a3e1845ce428781fe3b2fea58e521696caf0b`.
- `pnpm test extensions/codex/src/app-server/run-attempt.dynamic-tools.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`: **8/8 PASS**, measured command wall time **274.91s**, including module/compiled-worker initialization. The pending wait is virtual. Current-head hosted CI also passed this fixture's 8 tests; its measured test and job times are recorded below.
- `node scripts/check-changed.mjs --staged --base 24ca81d55bce94b26cb5c494e6987c39f2276081 -- extensions/codex/src/app-server/run-attempt.dynamic-tools.test.ts`: **PASS**, **1192.09s**. The canonical gate includes the complete extension-test type graph, changed-file typed lint (0 warnings/errors), formatting, ratchets and boundary/architecture guards. All three Knip scans passed with zero unused exports. No skip override was used. Source and staged tree stayed unchanged; no OOM was recorded.
- **Updated candidate real startup supplement: PASS, zero model turns.** Native Codex 0.160.0 completed real initialize and ephemeral thread/start calls through the production stdio client. The production Git-environment producer and transport preserved inherited Git configuration and appended the agent's maintenance settings in the actual native process. The effective thread used the selected supported provider. No app-server/process/clock mock, consumer login or credential copy was used. Native close returned `exited=true, cleanup=closed`, and the observed native PID identity was absent afterward. The bounded resource unit exited 0 in **101.18s**.
- Fresh independent P0–P2 source review verified the cleanup fix and found no remaining actionable P0–P2 issues in this candidate. Mandatory official AutoReview was run but produced **no validated report**: one 900s Codex timeout and a subsequent older-CLI attempt rejected the required isolation flag. Both remain `reviewer_unavailable`; usage/tokens are unknown. The current helper/native configuration cannot project the authorized local inference endpoint, so identical retries were stopped. These are tool-availability failures, not a clean AutoReview verdict.
- Original causal proof remains prior-head evidence: failed CI checkout `695a492a5d47ad8a911a094f11fa5c010b45e28e` and main parent `de2b8ae04af1623cbb5b72e84bb80976008b784f` reproduced **68 passed / 1 failed**, with the attempt budget expiring before native spawn. A fixture-only prototype on that parent passed **69/69**. [Original failed job](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/37760444620/job/113256012854).

**Previously completed real lifecycle proof is retained as evidence for old head `daf59eab1c1b1d8502f01801ade1ebaff0357102`, not relabelled as new-head live execution.** The budget, cancellation and process-supervisor owners are unchanged; the reachable native Git-startup change is covered by the new zero-turn supplement above. [ClawSweeper Revision 8](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/167409#issuecomment-6066951398) accepted the prior real proof and requested the main-clock integration now included.

| Prior-head real case | Result | Native turn / item | Explicit cancel | Interrupt request/response | Wall time |
| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Normal pending completion | PASS | completed / completed | 0 | 0/0 | 137.49s |
| Natural attempt expiry | PASS | interrupted / failed | 1 | 1/1 | 221.781s |
| Caller abort at actual READY | PASS | interrupted / failed | 1 | 1/1 | 85.302s |

Each final case ran production attempt → native managed Codex 0.160.0 → real model → production dynamic exec → native process, with one actual thread/start, turn/start, tool request and probe spawn. READY preceded result settlement; thread/turn/call bindings matched. Normal output appeared exactly once at stdout callback, tool response and native item boundaries. Timeout expired the 180,000ms production attempt budget (180.013s), including startup, while the 300s probe and 360s command budget remained pending and the caller signal stayed un-aborted. Caller abort fired no timeout. Both cancelled cases produced the expected failed tool/item, interrupted turn and timeout-versus-caller-abort projection.

The observed probe/ManagedRun PID identities were gone before app-server shutdown, and bounded units ended with zero remaining owned processes, no swap and no OOM increments. Prior-head native close remained `exited=true, cleanup=uncertain`; POSIX full-tree `waitForExtinction` was unavailable. Known-PID reaping and empty owned cgroups are not full-tree certification. No mocked model, client, supervisor, process or fake clock was used in these live cases.

Earlier proof failures remain qualified: the original consumer account route failed before any turn; an approval-registration failure occurred before probe spawn; an unsupported configuration was rejected before a turn; and a normal execution completed before its observer failed on incorrect optional extinction/output assumptions. Those observers were corrected against production contracts. Prior actual turn/start requests totalled 5 including failed attempts; billing cost is unknown. No additional model turn was needed for this main integration.

