## What Problem This Solves

Fixes memory search after an index written by v2026.11.5 under a non-English locale carries a legacy `scopeHash` that differs from the locale-independent hash.

Fixes #201808

## Why This Change Was Made

A configured scope mismatch now requests the normal search repair and rebuilds through the existing shadow-index publication path. Changed paths and patterns still invalidate the old corpus before search can serve it.

## User Impact

Users can recover existing indexes across locale changes while retaining indexed content; configuration changes still rebuild the correct corpus.

## Evidence

- Maintainer follow-up at `61f5471091fa8ea3e8aa5e62061c3791dc7d8b49`: serialized path entries now sort by UTF-16 code-unit order, so distinct composed/decomposed Unicode paths cannot compare equal and change the persisted hash with input order. A reverse-order regression covers both spellings. GitHub CI for that code head passed changed Node tests, type checks, lint, guards, and security-fast; the run was superseded by the docs update.
- Maintainer documentation follow-up at `9f5a12bd58b339720e34801ead84820831da514c`: the memory guide now explains automatic scope-only shadow rebuilds, potential embedding cost, and the separate explicit rebuild path for other identity changes. The branch merged current main at `fadb418fd3877a6bdbd2a2912d4317ba23d0714d` to preserve main’s generic memory-index wording; the PR diff remains six focused files. Exact-head CI run [45092139294](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/45092139294) attempt 2 passed, and the native GitHub gate accepted the squash merge at `b49b45a49bcd9d7c4d49d6f85a67ff9a53bdcbf0`.
- The CLI/Gateway trace and locale proof driver below were run on the earlier PR head `463b8147cf5e4f881313a8afc93db009c21c0376`. Their CJK path fixture is also covered by the updated regression, but the trace itself has not been rerun on the new head.
- `pnpm exec vitest run --maxWorkers=1 extensions/memory-core/src/memory/manager-search-upgrade.test.ts`: 17 passed, including a persisted v2026.11.5 zh-CN hash, reopen, retained chunks, and a changed-extra-path negative control.
- Real CLI/Gateway path using an isolated fixture: v2026.11.5 (`e13cf15`) wrote 3 files under zh-CN with legacy hash `976c4124…` (chunking 6, provenance 1). PR head `463b8147cf5e4f881313a8afc93db009c21c0376` under en-US recovered it; CLI search and Gateway `memory_search` each returned the CJK extra-path note and workspace note. The Gateway response marked the in-flight repair stale; after stopping Gateway and reopening the CLI, identity was valid with 3 files, 3 chunks, 3 sources, and `dirty=false`. Both CJK paths remained indexed; the recovered hash was `4717196e…`.
