## What Problem This Solves

Session-wide Stop can prepare unavailable storage for completed subagents that have no remaining work. The initial fix also dropped completed persistent children from descendant discovery, allowing a child accepted during another sibling's Stop drain to survive.

Related: #194252

## Why This Change Was Made

Keep completed roots in the existing cancellation scope and defer their session preparation until retained work appears. This preserves the descendant-refresh and completed-command cleanup contract introduced by `f61b347ee408569ec569a3f4a2f3a7383ea98fa5`; original session identity and cancellation authority checks still apply. Retained-work classification uses a read-only command-owner query sharing the cancellation selector, leaving cleanup-witness capture with the command cancellation owner.

The 122-line test allocation covers the removed-storage regression and retained-wake control without changing the shared budget baseline.

